1. src/baselines_new.py -- GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt).
   Contains a Python port of micd::gaussMItest from the R package micd
   (R. Foraita and R. Witte; GPL (>= 3)), implementing the multiple-imputation
   Fisher-z test of Witte, Foraita and Didelez (2022), used as the FZ-Rubin
   baseline.

2. src/notears_linear.py -- Apache-2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).
   Linear NOTEARS solver modified from https://github.com/xunzheng/notears
   (Zheng, Aragam, Ravikumar and Xing, 2018), Copyright the NOTEARS authors.
   Changes: covariance-form loss, equal-variance squared loss only, condensed
   into one function, called from the MissDAG M-step.

3. src/missdag_gaussian.py -- NOT REDISTRIBUTED.
   Derived from the public MissDAG code of Gao et al. (2022),
   https://github.com/ErdunGAO/MissDAG, whose repository specifies no
   licence. The file is excluded from the supplementary material and the public
   repository (release/MANIFEST.txt). Without it, run_missdag_gaussian raises an
   ImportError pointing to the original code.

Third-party software used but not redistributed (installed via environment.yml,
directly or as dependencies):
causal-learn (MIT; KCI and MVPC), scikit-learn, NumPy, SciPy, pandas (BSD-3),
LightGBM (MIT), XGBoost (Apache-2.0), networkx (BSD-3), matplotlib
(Matplotlib License, PSF-based), and the optional citest package (MIT;
https://github.com/MIDASverse/citest).

Data and network structures:
- Sachs et al. (2005) flow-cytometry data: not redistributed. data/fetch_sachs_data.sh
  downloads the copy distributed by the bnlearn repository
  (https://www.bnlearn.com/research/sachs05/) and checks it against the file
  used in the paper (shape, column names, value checksum).
- ALARM (Beinlich et al., 1989) and HAILFINDER (Abramson et al., 1996): only
  the published graph structures are used, hard-coded as edge lists in
  experiments/alarm.py and experiments/hailfinder.py; all data are simulated.
